WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:02.790
Every neighborhood has a house like it.

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:07.901
You can probably picture it: That old, decrepit
building on the very end of the street; it

00:00:07.901 --> 00:00:12.730
was there when you moved in, and it’ll still
be there when you move out.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:17.520
All sorts of salacious rumors spread about
houses like this - “it’s a drug lab”,

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:23.700
“it’s a hideout for fugitives”, “it’s
haunted” - but these are all just stories...right?

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.870
Some of these houses contain real nightmares,
though.

00:00:26.870 --> 00:00:29.060
Nightmares like SCP-136.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:34.750
There’s a grain of truth in every story,
and even lies can reveal certain facts about

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:35.750
their tellers.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:41.170
That’s why the SCP Foundation takes reports
of so-called neighborhood “haunted houses”

00:00:41.170 --> 00:00:45.850
seriously, and performs regular checks on
such buildings to see if any of them are actually

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.699
the real deal.

00:00:47.699 --> 00:00:52.890
Children can have wild imaginations - but
when children living on the same street, years

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:57.450
apart, with no reason to have been in contact
with one another, all start reporting an eerily

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:00.370
similar apparition in that creepy, old house.

00:01:00.370 --> 00:01:05.140
And when the stories go beyond just getting
freaked out, and delve into truly life-altering,

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:11.860
traumatic, paralytic terror… then the Foundation
really can’t afford not to look into it.

00:01:11.860 --> 00:01:17.340
One otherwise-quiet morning in a sleepy American
town, a convoy of fumigation and asbestos

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:22.530
removal trucks pulled in, surrounding that
creepy old house at the end of the street.

00:01:22.530 --> 00:01:26.570
Residents were probably thinking, “It’s
about time someone tore that old death-trap

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:30.659
down”, as people in protective suits spilled
into the building.

00:01:30.659 --> 00:01:35.759
These were, of course, Foundation Field agents,
who would perform a routine sweep around every

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:38.520
room, and fully catalogue the place.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:41.320
It looked like a pretty typical abandoned
house.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:46.670
Peeling wallpaper, dusty, rotten furniture,
all the trash and rubble that seems to appear

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:49.200
in the absence of human life.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.340
The full sweep took little more than an hour,
but towards the end of the observation period,

00:01:54.340 --> 00:02:00.200
Agent Sims - a field agent posted in the former
children’s bedroom - began acting strangely.

00:02:00.200 --> 00:02:03.460
He posed a question over the team’s shared
radio frequency.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:06.070
“Hey, can anyone else hear that laughter?”

00:02:06.070 --> 00:02:10.840
Confused, the other people on the team responded
that no, they could not hear any laughter.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:14.730
A few other agents came to check on the room,
but they didn’t hear any laughter in there

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:15.790
either.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:20.980
Even though Agent Sims appeared visibly uncomfortable,
there was no identifiable source for this

00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:22.010
discomfort.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:26.510
The other agents left him so they could continue
investigating the rest of the house.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:31.849
Other than one agent’s fraying nerves, there
didn’t appear to actually be anything anomalous

00:02:31.849 --> 00:02:33.470
about the house.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:38.370
Then Agent Sims screamed, and jumped out of
the second story window of the house, sailing

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:42.819
down towards the ground and fracturing his
spine on impact.

00:02:42.819 --> 00:02:44.450
What could have made him do that?

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:49.420
We’re talking about an SCP Foundation field
agent here - a highly-trained individual,

00:02:49.420 --> 00:02:54.010
hand-picked by the Foundation, to observe
and track terrifying and potentially deadly

00:02:54.010 --> 00:02:55.959
anomalies out in the field.

00:02:55.959 --> 00:03:00.290
What could he possibly have seen in that decrepit
old house that would lead him to believe leaping

00:03:00.290 --> 00:03:04.170
to his death was a preferable alternative
to facing it?

00:03:04.170 --> 00:03:08.870
This was a question that the Foundation absolutely
had to get an answer to.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:13.269
They intensified their search on the child’s
bedroom as the body of Agent Sims was carted

00:03:13.269 --> 00:03:14.269
away.

00:03:14.269 --> 00:03:20.049
That’s when they found the object that they
would later deem as SCP-136-1, a little rag

00:03:20.049 --> 00:03:22.310
doll made of old cloth.

00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:26.530
The kind of thing you could easily imagine
getting carted around by some ragamuffin child

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:29.000
at the turn of the last century.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:34.090
This was the only object of interest in the
entire room, so it was tagged, bagged, and

00:03:34.090 --> 00:03:38.659
taken back to the nearest Foundation containment
facility for further testing.

00:03:38.659 --> 00:03:41.870
They had no idea what they were about to unleash.

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:46.970
When the doll was first brought into its containment
chamber, one particular scientist on the research

00:03:46.970 --> 00:03:52.550
team - Dr. Meyers, a headstrong young researcher
freshly farmed from a prestigious university

00:03:52.550 --> 00:03:55.650
- took a morbid interest in the doll.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:04:00.140
Something about it, even in the absence of
readily apparent anomalous effects, made her

00:04:00.140 --> 00:04:02.549
feel oddly uncomfortable.

00:04:02.549 --> 00:04:05.970
The doll seemed to carry a vague aura of doom.

00:04:05.970 --> 00:04:09.079
Was this what made Agent Sims act the way
he had?

00:04:09.079 --> 00:04:11.370
Or was this only the beginning?

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:14.710
A D-Class was brought in for the first wave
of testing.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:18.870
The unfortunate former-arsonist was forced
to simply stand around in the room with the

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:24.120
doll and wait until something interesting
happened, and for twenty minutes, no anomalous

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:25.820
activity was reported.

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:30.270
Then, the D-Class began frantically looking
around the room, like a frightened animal.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:34.300
Dr. Meyers, who had been observing the test,
radioed in and asked what was happening.

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:35.690
“It’s this laughter.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:39.080
This weird, freaky laughter, like some crazy
lady is in here.

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:40.590
I can’t see her, though.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:41.610
Can any of you see her?

00:04:41.610 --> 00:04:42.610
Can any of you hear that?”

00:04:42.610 --> 00:04:44.860
They couldn’t see or hear anything.

00:04:44.860 --> 00:04:49.310
According to all their monitors, it was just
a lonely D-Class, standing around in an otherwise

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:52.190
empty room with nothing but the ragdoll.

00:04:52.190 --> 00:04:57.120
Five minutes after the D-Class reported hearing
the eerie laughter, he collapsed to the ground,

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:01.420
shrieking like a maniac and crawling away
from something he couldn’t see.

00:05:01.420 --> 00:05:05.590
He was emitting the desperate screams of a
man who truly believed something was about

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:09.169
to take his life, but nothing was there.

00:05:09.169 --> 00:05:13.889
He backed into the corner of the room, gibbering
incoherently and scratching desperately at

00:05:13.889 --> 00:05:19.500
the walls until his fingernails were ripping
off, leaving bloody traces behind.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:23.340
In the end, a pair of guards entered the chamber
and had to drag him out.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:28.259
The D-Class had urinated in fear, and seemed
to have temporarily lost the use of his legs

00:05:28.259 --> 00:05:29.539
from sheer panic.

00:05:29.539 --> 00:05:34.669
He was out of commission for several hours
afterwards, breaking into on-and-off screaming

00:05:34.669 --> 00:05:37.360
fits whenever someone approached him.

00:05:37.360 --> 00:05:42.039
Upon reviewing the footage of the experiment,
Dr. Meyers noticed something strange: The

00:05:42.039 --> 00:05:46.830
moment that the D-Class had begun screaming,
the doll had disappeared from the room.

00:05:46.830 --> 00:05:52.539
It only rematerialized in its previous position
when the D-Class was finally dragged from

00:05:52.539 --> 00:05:53.539
the room.

00:05:53.539 --> 00:05:56.960
Eventually, the D-Class became lucid enough
to be properly interviewed about his experience.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:02.440
He said that after first hearing the laughter,
a sense of overpowering dread had begun building

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:03.599
within him.

00:06:03.599 --> 00:06:10.889
Five minutes later, that was when the entity
- later dubbed SCP-136-2 - first appeared.

00:06:10.889 --> 00:06:15.360
The vision that appeared to him could generously
be described as human, but it was a little

00:06:15.360 --> 00:06:17.740
too tall to really qualify.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:22.610
The monster appeared to be female, but like
a freakish, carnival-house-of-mirrors exaggeration

00:06:22.610 --> 00:06:29.160
of what one thinks of being female - long,
flowing hair, large breasts, and a Barbie-Doll-Thin

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:30.160
waist.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:34.880
She looked like the nightmarish doodle of
a hormonal teen boy come to life, with a face

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:42.050
twisted into a rictus grin somewhere between
arousal and agony, showing way too many teeth.

00:06:42.050 --> 00:06:47.430
The creature was nude, and posed provocatively,
but it was anything but appealing.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:51.879
The D-Class reported that just seeing it was
the most frightening experience of his life…

00:06:51.879 --> 00:06:54.220
and then it started moving.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:58.780
It was slowly floating through the air towards
him like a vengeful ghost, that painful smile

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:01.600
getting wider as it drew closer to him.

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:05.530
The D-Class could only describe the whole
experience as feeling like death itself was

00:07:05.530 --> 00:07:07.090
coming towards him.

00:07:07.090 --> 00:07:10.870
When the creature was finally looming over
him as he cowered in the corner, it opened

00:07:10.870 --> 00:07:16.289
its tooth-lined jaws and let out a long, piercing
shriek, before disappearing.

00:07:16.289 --> 00:07:19.520
In the following weeks, the D-Class was kept
for testing.

00:07:19.520 --> 00:07:25.800
He experienced severe night terrors every
single night afterwards - all of them related

00:07:25.800 --> 00:07:27.139
to SCP-136.

00:07:27.139 --> 00:07:31.110
Further tests looked into the doll itself,
but there didn’t seem to be anything anomalous

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:32.790
about its construction.

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:36.720
It appeared to be made from the kind of plain,
non-anomalous materials you’d expect from

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:38.639
any doll of this variety.

00:07:38.639 --> 00:07:44.090
Though occasionally, the exact materials would
change, even between observers.

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:47.789
In addition to the most common “cloth”
variety, witnesses have reported the doll

00:07:47.789 --> 00:07:53.449
being made of clay, wood, and metal, with
10% viewing the doll as male, with the rest

00:07:53.449 --> 00:07:56.250
all agreeing that the doll is female.

00:07:56.250 --> 00:08:00.340
The Foundation conducted a battery of tests
on the doll, just to make sure that the results

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:03.259
were largely consistent across all subjects.

00:08:03.259 --> 00:08:10.050
Over 25 different subjects were tested on
SCP-136, all reporting roughly the same results:

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:14.940
Laughter after twenty minutes of observation,
a few minutes of silence, and then - according

00:08:14.940 --> 00:08:20.400
to subject testimonials - the appearance of
the same grinning, naked apparition, inducing

00:08:20.400 --> 00:08:23.819
a state of truly primal terror in its victims.

00:08:23.819 --> 00:08:29.030
Interestingly, not all of the subjects were
D-Classes: Some were volunteering scientists

00:08:29.030 --> 00:08:33.210
who were aware of the potential effects, but
let their morbid curiosity get the better

00:08:33.210 --> 00:08:38.360
of them, thinking they would be prepared to
face whatever terrifying vision would manifest

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:39.490
from the doll.

00:08:39.490 --> 00:08:44.410
But in every case, they were reduced to the
same screaming, traumatized wrecks.

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:51.380
But when a Foundation researcher named Dr.
Simon, the 25th subject of the SCP-136 experiments,

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:55.850
volunteered for testing, things took an even
more horrifying turn.

00:08:55.850 --> 00:09:00.930
During the testing period, Dr. Simon had the
unusual experience of not actually seeing

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:03.960
the SCP-136-2 entity.

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:08.080
After being told how terrifying it was by
coworkers, he was a little disappointed that

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:10.230
he didn’t get to share their fears.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:14.381
Later that day he went to get himself a warm
cup of coffee from the site’s employee break

00:09:14.381 --> 00:09:15.381
room.

00:09:15.381 --> 00:09:20.070
His coworkers became concerned when his coffee
mug dropped to the ground and shattered, as

00:09:20.070 --> 00:09:24.800
Dr. Simon pointed into a nearby empty hallway
and began screaming.

00:09:24.800 --> 00:09:30.250
He claimed that he could see her floating
down the hallway towards him, her face twisted

00:09:30.250 --> 00:09:32.530
into that menacing grin.

00:09:32.530 --> 00:09:36.250
As none of the other scientists could see
what Simon was seeing, they surrounded him

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:40.750
and attempted to calm him, assuming that he
was perhaps the victim of some kind of sudden,

00:09:40.750 --> 00:09:42.030
psychotic break.

00:09:42.030 --> 00:09:47.520
But minutes later, every scientist in the
break room collapsed and fell unconscious.

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:52.580
Not long after, they all began to wake back
up...Except Dr. Simon.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:57.060
He had fallen into a coma, and died while
still on life support three days later.

00:09:57.060 --> 00:10:03.140
It was the first report of SCP-136 causing
a death since Agent Sims’ unfortunate fall.

00:10:03.140 --> 00:10:08.980
Dr. Meyers immediately requested that SCP-136
be reclassified from Euclid to Keter Class

00:10:08.980 --> 00:10:12.810
so more resources could be allocated for its
containment.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:19.030
Administration denied any changes to the containment
procedures of SCP-136, frustrating Dr. Meyers,

00:10:19.030 --> 00:10:24.250
but little did she know that it was because
site administration had ulterior motives for

00:10:24.250 --> 00:10:26.210
SCP-136.

00:10:26.210 --> 00:10:30.590
No matter who they were, whether they were
the hardened killers of D-Class, the trained

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:35.520
soldiers of the Foundation field agent corps,
or jaded scientists who see any number of

00:10:35.520 --> 00:10:41.530
horrors each week as part of their normal
jobs, SCP-136 had the unique ability to reduce

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:44.160
its victims to terrified wrecks.

00:10:44.160 --> 00:10:49.330
In a move that feels decidedly more in line
with the Chaos Insurgency, site administration

00:10:49.330 --> 00:10:56.360
had started using SCP-136 to assist in enhanced
interrogation with detained people of interest.

00:10:56.360 --> 00:11:03.100
Even the toughest nuts to crack soon became
very talkative after the appearance of SCP-136-2

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:04.640
traumatized them for life.

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:10.350
Essentially, the administrators were making
a kind of deal with the devil: Allowing SCP-136

00:11:10.350 --> 00:11:15.460
more free reign, in exchange for them gathering
valuable intel from these victims.

00:11:15.460 --> 00:11:20.060
But as always, the problem with making deals
with the devil is that the devil is always

00:11:20.060 --> 00:11:22.510
going to collect his due in the end.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:27.700
Dr. Meyers’ warnings would continue to fall
upon deaf ears though, even as the creature’s

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.770
power seemed to grow.

00:11:29.770 --> 00:11:33.850
Tests on D-Classes continued, with the entity
traumatizing a whole group at once during

00:11:33.850 --> 00:11:35.690
one of these experiments.

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:40.140
However, when Dr. Meyers herself, along with
a few agents, entered the testing chamber

00:11:40.140 --> 00:11:43.640
to drag out their twitching bodies, they all
fell unconscious.

00:11:43.640 --> 00:11:50.040
When Dr. Meyers woke back up, three of the
D-Classes had fallen into comas like Dr. Simon,

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:51.760
and died shortly after.

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:56.790
Dr. Meyers pleaded with the administration
to terminate the doll, but her requests were

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:57.790
denied.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:12:01.670
It was proving to be too valuable in its various
interrogations.

00:12:01.670 --> 00:12:06.710
And besides, nobody was sure if the doll even
could be terminated.

00:12:06.710 --> 00:12:11.940
Whenever it was damaged, it simply disappeared
and reappeared within a one meter radius.

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:16.860
The only thing that hadn’t been tried was
full vaporization, which Dr. Meyers’ superiors

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:19.390
refused to sign off on.

00:12:19.390 --> 00:12:22.390
SCP-136 was here to stay.

00:12:22.390 --> 00:12:27.110
Unfortunately, the same could not be said
for Dr. Meyers herself.

00:12:27.110 --> 00:12:31.560
After one more unfortunate testing incident
where a D-Class disappeared entirely in what

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:37.740
seemed to be clear evidence of SCP-136’s
growing power, Dr. Meyers implored site administration

00:12:37.740 --> 00:12:41.500
to reclassify the anomaly and slate it for
termination.

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:46.050
It was getting more powerful, more unstable,
and more dangerous.

00:12:46.050 --> 00:12:51.370
But rather than terminate the anomalous ragdoll,
in the end all they did was remove Dr. Meyers

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.060
from the SCP-136 case.

00:12:54.060 --> 00:12:58.261
With her gone, there was one less thing for
them to worry about as they gave more and

00:12:58.261 --> 00:13:04.810
more victims to SCP-136, using its dark powers
to torture detained people of interest into

00:13:04.810 --> 00:13:07.640
telling them everything they wanted to know.

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:13.010
But with the entity seeming to grow more powerful
with every victim, it seems very likely that

00:13:13.010 --> 00:13:18.550
Dr. Meyers’ worst fears will come true,
and one day those controlling the terrifying

00:13:18.550 --> 00:13:23.850
anomaly will find that they’re the ones
hearing a strange, evil laughter coming from

00:13:23.850 --> 00:13:25.670
nowhere at all.

00:13:25.670 --> 00:13:31.890
Now check out “SCP-610 - The Flesh That
Hates” and “SCP-1337 - The Hitchhiker”

00:13:31.890 --> 00:13:34.350
for more SCPs that’ll chill you to the core!

